WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.813
Virtual appliances, vNIOS,
in each environment.

2
00:00:03.813 --> 00:00:09.174
On VMware, the OVA comes from Infoblox's
support site, which needs a login.

3
00:00:09.174 --> 00:00:12.777
Infoblox says not to change
the VM's settings in vSphere,

4
00:00:12.777 --> 00:00:17.788
because that may violate the virtual
licensing terms and stop the VM joining.

5
00:00:17.788 --> 00:00:21.479
Mixed SR-IOV and regular
network cards aren't supported,

6
00:00:21.479 --> 00:00:23.325
and cloned VMs aren't either.

7
00:00:23.325 --> 00:00:26.826
On Azure, marketplace deployment
is supported on Azure

8
00:00:26.826 --> 00:00:30.175
public and Azure Government,
with managed disks only.

9
00:00:30.175 --> 00:00:36.375
High availability arrived in 9.0.4, and
needs a custom role and a managed identity.

10
00:00:36.375 --> 00:00:42.439
The limits to plan around: DHCP failover
doesn't work behind NAT, there's no LAN2,

11
00:00:42.439 --> 00:00:47.839
no IPv6 high availability, and both
HA nodes must be in the same region,

12
00:00:47.839 --> 00:00:51.250
resource group,
availability zone and size.

13
00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:57.975
On AWS, high availability also starts at
9.0.4, and needs the VPC and subnets,

14
00:00:57.975 --> 00:01:05.037
an HA IAM role, and a Grid DNS resolver
that can reach the IAM and EC2 endpoints.

15
00:01:05.037 --> 00:01:10.712
Same limits: no IPv6 HA, same
region, zone and instance type.

16
00:01:10.712 --> 00:01:11.701
Now the gap.

17
00:01:11.701 --> 00:01:15.350
The HA prerequisites list
only commercial endpoints.

18
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.863
AWS lists the global and
China endpoints, not GovCloud.

19
00:01:19.863 --> 00:01:25.040
Azure lists management dot azure dot com
and login dot microsoftonline dot com,

20
00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.550
with no Azure Government equivalents.

21
00:01:27.550 --> 00:01:30.938
And failover time depends
on the cloud's own API.

22
00:01:30.938 --> 00:01:32.889
So ask Infoblox, in writing,

23
00:01:32.889 --> 00:01:37.413
before you rely on vNIOS failover
in either government cloud.

24
00:01:37.413 --> 00:01:40.063
One more constraint that shapes Part 2:

25
00:01:40.063 --> 00:01:43.212
vNIOS members can't
manage Microsoft servers.

26
00:01:43.212 --> 00:01:50.308
Sources: Infoblox vNIOS for VMware
installation guide (OVA, VM settings, SR-IOV);

27
00:01:50.308 --> 00:01:56.738
vNIOS for Azure (Marketplace support,
managed disks, HA prerequisites,

28
00:01:56.738 --> 00:02:02.835
custom role and managed identity,
limitations page version 19, Aug.

29
00:02:02.835 --> 00:02:07.935
31, 2026); vNIOS for AWS (HA
prerequisites and limitations);

30
00:02:07.935 --> 00:02:12.860
NIOS 9.1.x Guidelines for
managing Microsoft servers.
